      "solution": "$10 + 14 + 18 + 22 + \\dots + 138$ is arithmetic with $u_1 = 10$, $d = 4$\nNow $u_1 + (n - 1)d = 138$\n$10 + 4(n - 1) = 138$\n$4(n - 1) = 128$\n$n - 1 = 32$\n$n = 33$\nSo, the sum is $\\frac{n}{2}(u_1 + u_{33}) = \\frac{33}{2}(10 + 138) = \\frac{33}{2}(148) = 2442$",
